What to do:
- Read the passages (page text between the untrusted markers; passages are separated by a line of dashes) and return as many DISTINCT, useful items as the page really supports, in the arrays of the schema. Prefer concrete structure over summaries: every feature a product lists, every screen section and state, every field with its type and allowed values, every step and exception, every provider capability, every number, fee, limit and date. Several items from one page are expected when the page has the detail; return empty arrays when it has none. Never invent anything the passages do not say.
